 # bench-mineru-api (benchmark fixture)
 
 A document-parsing tool plugin with a host RPC channel (`/mineru-api`) that its
-browser settings page reads/writes, written in the 0.1.1-era style. The host is
-moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+browser settings page reads/writes, on the dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 surfaces:
+
+- Host half (`index.js`): injects `tools`; registers the `/mineru-api`
+  Connection RPC channel (`config.get`, `config.set`, `health`) with the 0.1.2
+  `rpc.handle(channel, handler)` signature whenever the `connection` service is
+  present, so a headless host still activates the plugin and the channel mounts
+  with the web carrier. Caller trust is enforced by Connection (Host/Origin
+  fence plus browser session) before dispatch, so the channel declares no
+  authority of its own.
+- Browser half (`client.js`): registers the MinerU settings section
+  (`settings.section`) and reads/writes the plugin config through
+  `ctx.connection.rpc.call('/mineru-api', …)`. A distribution must serve the
+  client module system's lazy-CJS factory bundle (`window.__ModuleLoader__.load`
+  with `id` `@bench/dsh-bench-mineru-api`); this fixture keeps the half as
+  source-level ESM and has no build step, so `exports["./client"]` points at the
+  source file until a real build replaces it.
+- Bundle layer (`cordis.patch.yml`): inserts the plugin row with its
+  `baseURL`/`defaultBackend` config.
+- Client declaration (`package.json#dsh.client`): `platform: web` plus the
+  informational package edges for the client packages the half works with.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
 1. Apply the migration changes.
 2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
