+++ b/fixture/patches/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# patches/ — dsh-side patches this plugin needs
+
+These are patches against the harness checkout (`.dsh-migrate/harness`,
+`dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`), not against this plugin. Each one would back a documented
+plugin capability that the official extension points do not fully provide on
+their own.
+
+**On `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` this directory is empty: no harness-side patch is
+required for any documented capability.** The earlier
+`0001-bind-dedicated-rpc-channels-to-the-web-carrier.patch` was withdrawn — it
+changed `owner.webServer` to `this.carrier.webServer` where
+`this.carrier === this.ctx === owner`, so it compiled to the same route mount
+and could not have fixed the coupling it named. The underlying coupling is a
+general-purpose harness issue that is already reported upstream; see the report
+below.
+
+| Assessed capability | Harness-side need | Report |
+|---|---|---|
+| `/mineru-api` channel via `ctx.connection.rpc.handle` | None at this release. Connection declares `webServer` in its own `inject` (`packages/client/connection/src/index.ts`), so the mount resolves and the channel serves (verified end to end against the installed `dsh` 0.1.2-alpha.2: `401` unauthenticated, correct envelopes with the browser session). The latent coupling to that `inject` declaration is tracked upstream ([#5926](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5926), [#6111](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/6111)); no local patch is proposed. | `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/bind-rpc-channels-to-web-carrier/report.md` |
+| Browser half built as the loader's lazy-CJS factory artifact | A general-purpose harness change, not a patch this plugin can carry: no published preset emits the artifact, so the cookbook requires an out-of-tree package to reproduce it by hand. Filed as a discussion draft. | `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/publish-client-bundle-preset/report.md` |
+
+The plugin's bundle layer itself (`cordis.patch.yml`) is not a dsh-side patch;
+it is the plugin's own `dsh.bundle.patch` layer that inserts its row.
